    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with **Vinnie Pasquantino** leading the charge, posting a massive 76.21 efficiency score against Max Scherzer. This is our clearest play; while the veteran SP carries name recognition, his 5.31 xERA dictates an aggressive start, and **Vinnie Pasquantino**\u2019s substantial platoon advantage (+14%) makes him the anchor of our lineup. **Corbin Carroll** (74.41) and **Seiya Suzuki** (64.62) follow closely behind. While **Corbin Carroll** deals with a slight efficiency tax due to Clay Holmes's elite hold ability, his speed profile and #2 slotting keep his floor elevated. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a positive SP skill matchup against Brandon Pfaadt and provides a strong pivot if you are hunting for multi-category contributions in a favorable hitting environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench despite a respectable 43.98 score. While he brings high sprint speed and a favorable platoon edge against Ian Seymour, his overall base projection couldn't overcome the drag of a -19% SP skill penalty, pushing him just below our threshold for starting consideration. We also continue to monitor the status of **Austin Riley**, who sits on the bench today with a 42.81 rating; despite his pedigree, the matchup against Tyler Glasnow is simply too volatile for a high-leverage Roto start. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board. Be particularly wary of **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 54.51 is tethered to a significant -15% platoon hit against Andrew Alvarez; if the lineup shuffles, we may pivot to a bench option to preserve precious game caps. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** represents a high-ceiling, low-floor play against Ethan Pecko\u2014while his 55.35 score is buoyed by a +19% SP skill advantage, his bottom-of-the-order placement significantly caps his R/RBI potential. We are proceeding with the current construction, but keep an eye on **Henry Bolte** and **Gabriel Moreno** for late-afternoon adjustments should weather or confirmed batting orders shift their projected value.",
